      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nOn ROCm, MXFP4 MoE auto-selection now offers `TRITON_UNFUSED` between `AITER_MXFP4_BF16` and `EMULATION`, so CDNA2 (gfx90a, MI210/MI250X) gets the native OAI Triton kernels instead of emulation. Fixes #59151.\n\n## Claims\n\n- On gfx90a, `select_deepseek_v4_mxfp4_moe_backend()` (the generic MXFP4 path used by `Mxfp4MoEMethod`) picks `TRITON_UNFUSED` instead of `EMULATION`.\n- One-line change to the ROCm priority list; no change on CUDA/XPU/CPU.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test `test_rocm_mxfp4_moe_selects_triton_unfused_without_aiter` in `tests/kernels/moe/test_ocp_mx_moe.py` runs the real oracle on ROCm with AITER disabled (runs in the MI300 MoE Kernels CI step).\n\nOn 1x MI250X GCD (gfx90a), vLLM v0.31.0 ROCm image with this change bind-mounted:\n\n```\npytest tests/kernels/moe/test_ocp_mx_moe.py::test_rocm_mxfp4_moe_selects_triton_unfused_without_aiter\n# without this change:\nE       AssertionError: assert <Mxfp4MoeBackend.EMULATION: 'EMULATION'> == <Mxfp4MoeBackend.TRITON_UNFUSED: 'TRITON_UNFUSED'>\n1 failed\n# with this change:\n1 passed\n```\n\nFull `tests/kernels/moe/test_ocp_mx_moe.py` on the same GCD: the set of failing tests is identical with and without this change (22, all pre-existing on this hardware/image: emulation, CUTLASS EP and gfx950 round-up tests), except the new test.\n\nEnd to end, `TRITON_UNFUSED` serves Kimi-K3 (MXFP4) on 4 nodes x 8 MI250X GCDs (selected explicitly there, because compressed-tensors MXFP4 goes through the gpt-oss priority list); see #63978. The issue reporter ran MiMo-V2.6-Flash on 4x MI210 with the backend forced.\n\n## Details\n\n- Root cause: `_get_priority_backends()` on ROCm listed only `AITER_MXFP4_BF16` and `EMULATION`. AITER's MXFP4 MoE kernels require CDNA3+, while `UnfusedOAITritonExperts` already reports gfx90a as supported (`_triton_kernel_moe_supports_current_device()`).\n- Tradeoff: CDNA3/CDNA4 with AITER disabled (the default, `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0`) also move from `EMULATION` to `TRITON_UNFUSED` for this path. With AITER enabled, `AITER_MXFP4_BF16` still wins.\n- Not a duplicate: #54202 re-enables `TRITON_UNFUSED` in the gpt-oss list (`_get_priority_backends_for_gpt_oss()`); this PR changes the generic ROCm list. No open PR references #59151.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
